{"nodes": [{"id": "design_v3_00_intake_backlog_intake_backlog", "label": "v3 Intake Backlog (founder list, 9 Jul 2026)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "design/v3/00-intake-backlog.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "All 31 (plus a 32nd second-intake) items are kept verbatim and mapped to an owning doc \u2014 nothing is dropped, so the founder can audit that every ask has a home."}, {"id": "design_v3_00_intake_backlog_cluster_summary", "label": "v3 cluster summary (trust / shell / funnel / explain / operate / grow)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "design/v3/00-intake-backlog.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Clustering 32 scattered asks into six themes maps them onto PROMPT-30..39 so the wave order follows a narrative (fix trust before fixing the funnel) instead of intake order."}, {"id": "design_v3_00_intake_backlog_in_app_stripe_no_portal", "label": "In-built Stripe: no Customer Portal for any billing flow", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "design/v3/00-intake-backlog.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Second-intake decision (9 Jul): cancel/resume, card update via Elements, invoices and interval switch all move in-app and /api/billing/portal is deleted, so the billing experience never leaves the product."}, {"id": "design_v3_00_intake_backlog_metered_event_pricing", "label": "Per-event metered pricing (market-validated)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "design/v3/00-intake-backlog.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Validated against Tournify's EUR40/EUR120 single-use upgrades \u2014 an organiser running one tournament a year should not need a subscription."}, {"id": "design_v3_00_inta